---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<BaseLayout
  title="NO BALL GAMES Lore | Characters, Signs, Streets & Restricted Zones"
  description="Enter the NO BALL GAMES lore archive: signs, streets, characters, restricted zones, secret games and the mythology behind the street-culture brand."
  current="lore"
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <span class="eyebrow">Lore archive</span>
    <h1>The sign was only the first warning.</h1>
    <p>
      NO BALL GAMES works as a full story world. The banned court, the blocked estate, the painted wall and the secret game all become part of the mythology. This is where the brand builds its universe.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-header">
      <h2>The world so far</h2>
      <p>Four phases of the NO BALL GAMES universe.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="timeline">
      <article class="timeline-item">
        <strong>Origin</strong>
        <div>
          <h3>The sign</h3>
          <p>A public warning designed to stop play becomes the central symbol of the brand. Yellow enamel, bold letters, screwed to a wall — and completely ignored by everyone who matters.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="timeline-item">
        <strong>Phase one</strong>
        <div>
          <h3>The wall</h3>
          <p>The message moves from sign to surface: tags, grime texture, characters, posters, stencils and coded marks. The wall talks back.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="timeline-item">
        <strong>Phase two</strong>
        <div>
          <h3>The players</h3>
          <p>Characters emerge from the restricted zones. Each one carries a different version of rebellion, humour, survival or creative defiance. They live in the gaps between the rules.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="timeline-item">
        <strong>Phase three</strong>
        <div>
          <h3>The movement</h3>
          <p>The brand becomes a hub for collectors, artists, gamers, writers and supporters who understand the meaning behind the phrase. <a class="inline-link" href={`${base}community/`}>Join the community →</a></p>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-header">
      <h2>Character previews</h2>
      <p>The restricted zones produce their own cast. More coming as the world expands.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card-grid">
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="kicker">Character</span>
        <h3>The Warden</h3>
        <p>Enforcer of the sign. Clips it to every fence, every gate, every blank wall — but never sticks around to see it ignored. The symbol of empty authority.</p>
        <div class="coming-soon-tag">Full profile coming soon</div>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="kicker">Character</span>
        <h3>The Tagger</h3>
        <p>First one in, last one out. Turns restrictions into canvases. Leaves something on every surface the Warden ever cleared.</p>
        <div class="coming-soon-tag">Full profile coming soon</div>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="kicker">Character</span>
        <h3>The Collector</h3>
        <p>Archives everything — signs, tags, photos, fragments, stories. Believes the culture should be preserved not erased. The memory of the movement.</p>
        <div class="coming-soon-tag">Full profile coming soon</div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section split-grid">
    <article class="panel-card">
      <span class="kicker">World ingredients</span>
      <h2>Simple objects. Bigger meaning.</h2>
      <p>
        The lore stays grounded in familiar British visual language: signs, fences, courts, alleyways, estate blocks, shutters, bus stops, school walls and concrete spaces. The extraordinary hides inside the ordinary.
      </p>
      <a class="inline-link" href={`${base}collections/`}>Collect from the world →</a>
    </article>
    <article class="panel-card">
      <span class="kicker">Lore tags</span>
      <div class="tag-cloud">
        <span>restricted zones</span><span>secret games</span><span>estate mythology</span><span>graffiti codes</span><span>street characters</span><span>blocked courts</span><span>urban folklore</span><span>collector lore</span><span>the sign</span><span>the wall</span><span>the players</span><span>the movement</span>
      </div>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="section cta-block">
    <div class="cta-block-inner">
      <span class="eyebrow">Lore grows with the community</span>
      <h2>Help build the world.</h2>
      <p>Characters, stories, restricted zones and coded messages need people to carry them forward. Follow, collect and contribute to keep the mythology alive.</p>
      <div class="cta-row">
        <a class="button primary" href={`${base}community/`}>Join the community</a>
        <a class="button secondary" href={`${base}collections/`}>Collect the culture</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
